From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:44:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] WindowManager Jetpack: a placeholder waits for its primary to
 resume

When the launcher brings a split task to the front, the server clears
the placeholder's TaskFragment. Its container is cleaned up and the
primary's, now on top, is updated at once, which launches a new
placeholder. That callback and the primary's own NewIntent+Resume both
land on the main thread, in whichever order they arrived. When the
callback wins, the placeholder is created, resumed and drawn before the
primary resumes: Settings opens with its right pane alone and the
launcher showing through the left for a few hundred milliseconds
(216 ms on mocha, 1 launch in 24).

A container made top by a cleanup is now updated once its top activity
has resumed, from onActivityPostResumed, and at once if it already has.
Android 13 and 14 launch the placeholder the same way and do not wait
either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../extensions/embedding/SplitController.java | 38 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../extensions/embedding/SplitPresenter.java  |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitController.java b/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitController.java
index fc95592..272cc4c 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitController.java
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitController.java
@@ -68,6 +68,10 @@ public class SplitController implements JetpackTaskFragmentOrganizer.TaskFragmen
     // We currently only support split activity embedding within the one root Task.
     private final Rect mParentBounds = new Rect();
 
+    // A container whose update waits for its top activity to resume.
+    @Nullable
+    private TaskFragmentContainer mContainerAwaitingResume;
+
     public SplitController() {
         mPresenter = new SplitPresenter(new MainThreadExecutor(), this);
         ActivityThread activityThread = ActivityThread.currentActivityThread();
@@ -450,6 +454,35 @@ public class SplitController implements JetpackTaskFragmentOrganizer.TaskFragmen
         mPresenter.updateSplitContainer(splitContainer, container, wct);
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Updates the container the way {@link #updateContainer} does, but not before its top
+     * activity has resumed. Cleaning up a container makes the one below it top, and updating
+     * that one can launch its placeholder: when the launcher brings the task to the front, the
+     * placeholder's container is cleared and the primary is updated while its own resume is
+     * still on its way. Launched then, the placeholder is created, resumed and drawn before the
+     * primary resumes, and the split shows its secondary half alone for a few frames.
+     */
+    void updateContainerOnceResumed(@NonNull WindowContainerTransaction wct,
+            @NonNull TaskFragmentContainer container) {
+        final Activity topActivity = container.getTopNonFinishingActivity();
+        if (topActivity != null && !topActivity.isResumed()) {
+            mContainerAwaitingResume = container;
+            return;
+        }
+        updateContainer(wct, container);
+    }
+
+    private void onActivityResumed(@NonNull Activity activity) {
+        final TaskFragmentContainer container = mContainerAwaitingResume;
+        if (container == null || container.isFinished()
+                || container.getTopNonFinishingActivity() != activity) {
+            return;
+        }
+        mContainerAwaitingResume = null;
+        mPresenter.updateContainer(container);
+        updateCallbackIfNecessary();
+    }
+
     /**
      * Returns the top active split container that has the provided container, if available.
      */
@@ -771,6 +804,11 @@ public class SplitController implements JetpackTaskFragmentOrganizer.TaskFragmen
             SplitController.this.onActivityCreated(activity);
         }
 
+        @Override
+        public void onActivityPostResumed(Activity activity) {
+            SplitController.this.onActivityResumed(activity);
+        }
+
         @Override
         public void onActivityConfigurationChanged(Activity activity) {
             SplitController.this.onActivityConfigurationChanged(activity);
diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitPresenter.java b/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitPresenter.java
index ade5731..44ee22e 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitPresenter.java
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Jetpack/src/androidx/window/extensions/embedding/SplitPresenter.java
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ class SplitPresenter extends JetpackTaskFragmentOrganizer {
 
         final TaskFragmentContainer newTopContainer = mController.getTopActiveContainer();
         if (newTopContainer != null) {
-            mController.updateContainer(wct, newTopContainer);
+            mController.updateContainerOnceResumed(wct, newTopContainer);
         }
 
         applyTransaction(wct);
